        title: 'Product Overview',
        content:
          'The Instant Photo Booth Screen is designed around a simple behavioural truth: people will pose for a camera, but they will stay for a wall. Traditional photo booths capture an image and hand it over, and the moment ends there. This installation deliberately separates capture from display, so the photograph becomes a public event. A guest takes their picture at a compact tablet station, and within seconds that image appears on a large LED wall or projection surface that everyone in the room can see, joining a growing mosaic of everyone who came before them.\n\nThat delay of a few seconds is the whole mechanic. Guests do not walk away after capture; they turn around and wait for their photo to arrive on the wall. Their friends watch with them. Passers-by look at the wall, see the queue, and join it. The installation therefore generates three distinct forms of engagement from a single interaction: the capture itself, the collective anticipation, and the spectator pull of a wall that keeps changing. Very few activations produce that much visible energy from such a small physical footprint.\n\nThe capture station is intentionally minimal. Nebuloid uses a securely mounted tablet in a brand-matched stand with a clear call to action, front-facing capture, an optional countdown, and a live preview. The guest journey is typically three taps: start, capture, and confirm. Consent language is presented before capture, and where you want contact details the form is kept to the smallest possible number of fields so the queue never stalls. Group shots, retakes, and multiple frame choices are all supported without adding complexity to the flow.\n\nBranding is applied at the moment of capture rather than in post-production. Every image is composited with your campaign frame, logo lockup, event date, hashtag, and any dynamic elements such as session names or sponsor bands. Because the frame is burned into the file that the guest receives and shares, every onward post carries your identity intact, which is what converts a hundred guests into thousands of impressions across their networks.\n\nThe wall layer is fully art-directed. Nebuloid builds the display as a designed canvas rather than a default slideshow: photos can drop into a growing mosaic, tile into a shaped logo, flow through a carousel with kinetic typography, or fill a themed scene that matches the stage design. Recency logic keeps the newest photo prominent for a few seconds so guests always see theirs arrive, then folds it into the collective wall. Moderation runs continuously, with automatic content checks and an operator override so nothing inappropriate ever reaches the screen.\n\nDelivery and data close the loop. Guests receive their photo instantly through a QR code, WhatsApp, or email, which is also the natural point to capture an opt-in for follow-up. The platform records captures, deliveries, share actions, peak activity windows, and consented contacts, and the full gallery is handed over after the event as a branded asset for your channels. What you end up with is not just a fun corner of the venue but a measurable acquisition and amplification channel with a permanent content library attached.',
